ipserv_fp8, dietgpu_fp8,\n    57\t# p3flat_fp8) quantize, so offload_compressed prefill must keep their\n    58\t# uncompressed copy (see the \"for accuracy\" branch in _get_weight_source).\n    59\t_LOSSLESS_OFFLOAD_CODECS = frozenset({\n    60\t    \"zipserv\", \"dietgpu\", \"zipserv_bf16\", \"dietgpu_bf16\",\n    61\t    \"p4flat\", \"p4d16\", \"ublb_flat\",\n    62\t    \"chunk_delta3\",\n    63\t})\n    64\t\n    65\t# Phase-adaptive prefill for offload_compressed weights (see _get_weight_source).\n    66\t# offload_compressed already keeps BOTH a compressed and an uncompressed LPDDR\n    67\t# copy; today prefill ALWAYS H2Ds the uncompressed one (no chunk gating). Below\n    68\t# this per-codec chunk threshold, prefill instead H2Ds + FULL-decompresses the\n    69\t# compressed copy. Same slack model as the frozen_split knob\n    70\t# (thr = (T_load_raw - T_decomp)/T_gemm_per_token) but with DISTINCT inputs:\n    71\t# offload does the FULL-blob decompress (vs frozen_split's cheap exp-only), so\n    72\t# T_decomp is much larger, AND offload configs (e.g. flexgen-comp) typically\n    73\t# keep half the layers frozen_uncompressed, so fewer layers load -> smaller\n    74\t# T_load_raw. Both shrink the slack -> a MUCH lower threshold than frozen_split.\n    75\t#   codec    thr   source\n    76\t#   zipserv  384   flexgen-comp slack model: load_raw 182 / full decomp 109 ->\n    77\t#                  slack 73 -> 384 (vs cao's 1330 — same codec, different config).\n    78\t# Codecs without an entry resolve to 0 (disabled = always-uncompressed prefill,\n    79\t# i.e. unchanged behaviour). Per-config; override via\n    80\t# TIERED_SERVE_OFFLOAD_PREFILL_MAX_CHUNK (same \"<codec>=<n>,...|<int>\" syntax).\n    81\t_OFFLOAD_PREFILL_MAX_CHUNK_DEFAULTS = {\n    82\t    \"zipserv\": 384,   # flexgen-comp (offload, full decompress -> small slack)\n    83\t}\n    84\t\n    85\t_ENV_FROZEN_DETAILED_NVTX = (\n    86\t    os.getenv(\"TIERED_SERVE_FROZEN_DETAILED_NVTX\", \"0